Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 17:15:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: build FH2 Recompiled's native renderer in, off by
 default

scripts/prepare.sh copies FH2 Recompiled's native renderer (app/src/nativo,
from NFSMW Android Evolved's) into forza-recomp/src/nativo. It is built
with FH2's branches, since FH2 on the Xbox 360 runs on FH1's engine, and a
few FH1 answers:

- the app takes its graphics system with nfsmw_renderizador = nativo, as
  FH2 Recompiled's does; the GPU plugin is not loaded then;
- the TU4 shader constructors and the vertex fetch patcher are hooked at
  FH2's addresses shifted the way the rest of the D3D library is (weak
  references, so a missing function still links);
- vertex shaders whose exports D3D relinked or nulled are matched to
  their containers (the rules of ReImagined's fxobj_shaders.py);
- ReIGlue's presenter has no frame generation and its settings overlay
  cannot hide entries: those calls are left out;
- the shader library is fh1_shaders.nfsp.

The host compile check builds it with the same definitions.
